        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "M4111-C",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "prompt": "C. A terminology curator has two published journal papers defining regional max pooling and one other paper proposing a component named Temporal Reliability Pooling. The curator wants to register the full latter name as a general mechanism and give it the Chinese name 年龄门控 because a machine translator suggested it. Is that justified? Explain what evidence each decision needs. The same author has an accurately defined new module of their own and wants to name it in their manuscript; explain whether the same admission requirement prohibits that.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Check full-name semantic evidence independently of the base operation.",
        "Require independent reliable Chinese translation evidence and distinguish a new author-proposed name."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Count partial-name pooling sources as proof of the proposed full category.",
        "Accept a machine translation as verified or prohibit all new names."
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4111-revised.md",
